'''Naoto Kongo''' ({{nihongo|金剛 直人|Kongō Naoto}}, born March 15, 1991) is a former Lurandian Football linebacker and current professional bodybuilder. He played his entire eight-year X-League career (2012–2019) for the [[Okami Direwolves]], where he established himself as the most dominant middle linebacker of his generation and the spiritual core of the Direwolves' famed {{nihongo|"Iron Curtain"|鉄のカーテン|Tetsu no Kāten}} defense. A three-time Division 1 Defensive Player of the Year and the 2015 Rice Bowl MVP, Kongo retired at age 28 in January 2020 to pursue competitive bodybuilding full-time, a decision rooted in the {{nihongo|[[Cult of Iron]]|鉄身信仰|Tesshin-shinkō}} tradition that shaped his athletic identity from childhood.

In bodybuilding, Kongo won the [[Iron Sakura Classic]] in 2022 and 2023 and the [[Okaiken National Grand Prix]] in 2024, becoming one of the few athletes to reach the pinnacle of both Lurandian Football and the Forge State's national bodybuilding circuit.

==Early life==
Kongo was born in [[Toyozawa]], [[Okaiken]], and grew up in the city's industrial Kita-Kawara district, the son of a steelworker and a physical education instructor. His father, Hiroshi Kongo, had been a regional [[Goriki]] competitor in his youth and instilled the {{nihongo|[[Cult of Iron]]|鉄身信仰|Tesshin-shinkō}} philosophy in his son from an early age: the body is a forge, the iron is the will, and discipline is the hammer.

[[File:Toyozawa Kita-Kawara district.png|thumb|left|The Kita-Kawara industrial district of Toyozawa, where Kongo grew up]]

Kongo began playing Lurandian Football at age 10 with the Kita-Kawara Junior Warriors, a community youth program. By 14, he was starting at linebacker for Toyozawa North High School and had already developed the punishing tackling style and sideline-to-sideline range that would define his professional career. He was named the Iron Helmet Tournament Most Valuable Defensive Player in 2008, his junior year, attracting attention from every major university program in the country.

As a teenager, Kongo also trained at the [[Toyozawa Iron Temple]], a gym owned by former Goriki competitor [[Goro Takada|"The Anvil" Takada]]. The gym served as a cultural hub for the {{nihongo|Forge State|鍛冶国家|Kaji Kokka}} ideology, and Kongo's exposure to bodybuilders, Goriki athletes, and strength athletes there shaped his understanding of the iron as both physical tool and spiritual practice—a duality that would define his two-sport career.

==College career==
Kongo accepted a full athletic scholarship to [[Okami Teikoku University]], choosing the storied program over offers from Keio University and Toyozawa University. As a freshman in 2009, he won the starting middle linebacker position in training camp and never relinquished it. Over three seasons (2009–2011), Kongo recorded 287 tackles, 14 sacks, and 5 interceptions, earning three consecutive Kanto Collegiate Gaikyū League All-Star selections and the 2011 Scholar's Bowl Defensive MVP.

[[File:Okami Teikoku University campus.png|thumb|Okami Teikoku University, where Kongo played collegiate Lurandian Football]]

His 2011 season—112 tackles, 6 sacks, and 2 interceptions in 10 games—cemented his status as the top defensive prospect in X-League draft history to that point. He declared for the X-League Draft following his junior year, forgoing his final season of eligibility.

